This folder contains module tests for Simu5G: small simulations, each checking
one behavior of a module or a few modules working together, by the outcome of
the run (its output, its exit code, its error message). They complement the
fingerprint tests (tests/fingerprint), which guard the example simulations
against unintended change, and the unit tests (tests/unit), which exercise
classes without a running simulation. The example simulations under
simulations/ all run to completion; a configuration that must be rejected is
tested here instead.

Each *.test file is an opp_test test case: it defines the network in a %file
section or takes one from lib/, gives its configuration in an %inifile section,
and states what the run must produce (%exitcode, %contains, ...).

Running the tests
-----------------

    ./runtest                # all tests, against the release library
    ./runtest Foo.test ...   # selected tests
    MODE=debug ./runtest     # against the debug library

or, from the project root,

    make moduletests
    make MODE=debug moduletests

Both the Simu5G and the INET shared library must be built in the requested
mode, and SIMU5G_ROOT and INET_ROOT must be set (source the setenv script of
both projects). The generated files and the captured output of each run end
up in ./work, which is not under version control.

Writing tests
-------------

A test may also carry C++ code in %file sections (e.g. a module subclass that
stands for another configuration policy): the runner compiles the C++ of all
tests into one executable, linked with the Simu5G and INET libraries, and runs
every test on it. lib/ holds the networks several tests share (package
simu5g.test.moduletest.lib) and defaults.ini, which a test's omnetpp.ini
includes:

    include ../../lib/defaults.ini

A test of a rejected configuration expects exit code 1 and checks the error
message on stderr, so that an error of another cause fails the test.
